<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Spanish Louisiana</h1><p class="st-meta">1762 CE – 1803 CE · capital New Orleans</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spain's vast Mississippi province, ruled from New Orleans for four decades before Napoleon took it back and sold it to the United States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the secret <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fontainebleau-1762">Treaty of Fontainebleau</a> of 1762 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> handed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-louisiana">French Louisiana</a> west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, to its ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> as compensation for losses in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. Spanish authority arrived slowly: the first governor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-ulloa">Antonio de Ulloa</a>, was driven out by French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> rebels in 1768, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alejandro-oreilly">Alejandro O'Reilly</a> crushed the revolt in 1769.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> was governed as a dependency of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/captaincy-general-of-cuba">Captaincy General of Cuba</a>, under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-spain">New Spain</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> kept French law and the French-speaking elite largely in place, welcomed Acadian refugees and Canary Islanders, and opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> to trade. Plantations grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> with enslaved African labour. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-de-galvez">Bernardo de Gálvez</a> used the colony as a base to seize British posts in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-west-florida">Province of West Florida</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-treaty-of-san-ildefonso">Treaty of San Ildefonso</a> in 1800 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> secretly returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Spanish officials still governed until 1803, when the colony was handed to France and, weeks later, to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana-purchase">Louisiana Purchase</a>, doubling American territory.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/spanish-louisiana.jpg" alt="Spanish Louisiana" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: althistory.wikia.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louisiana_(1762)_orthographic_projection.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1762 CE – 1803 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Orleans</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alejandro O'Reilly, Bernardo de Gálvez, Esteban Rodríguez Miró</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Luisiana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1782&amp;focus=spanish-louisiana" aria-label="Spanish Louisiana on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2339 1083 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Spanish Louisiana